{"cut_proposal":{"candidate_errors":[],"prefix":"To determine the value of \\(p + q\\), we need to find the equation of the line that passes through the given points. We start by identifying two points from the table to find the slope of the line. The points \\((2, -5)\\) and \\((p, -14)\\) can be used to find the slope \\(m\\).\n\nThe slope \\(m\\) is given by:\n\\[\nm = \\frac{y_2 - y_1}{x_2 - x_1} = \\frac{-14 - (-5)}{p - 2} = \\frac{-14 + 5}{p - 2} = \\frac{-9}{p - 2}\n\\]\n\nNext, we use the point-slope form of the line equation \\(y - y_1 = m(x - x_1)\\) with the point \\((2, -5)\\):\n\\[\ny + 5 = \\frac{-9}{p - 2}(x - 2)\n\\]\nSimplifying, we get:\n\\[\ny = \\frac{-9}{p - 2}(x - 2) - 5\n\\]\n\n","prefix_end":619,"status":"review_required"},"eligible":false,"generation":{"generation":{"max_new_tokens":2048,"temperature":0.7,"top_k":0,"top_p":1.0},"ids":[1249,8253,279,897,315,17767,79,488,2804,59,701,582,1184,311,1477,279,23606,315,279,1555,429,16211,1526,279,2661,3501,13,1205,1191,553,24588,1378,3501,504,279,1965,311,1477,279,30232,315,279,1555,13,576,3501,1124,1188,17,11,481,20,10699,8,323,1124,1188,79,11,481,16,19,10699,8,646,387,1483,311,1477,279,30232,17767,76,59,3593,785,30232,17767,76,57758,374,2661,553,510,59,9640,76,284,1124,37018,90,88,62,17,481,379,62,16,15170,87,62,17,481,856,62,16,92,284,1124,37018,19999,16,19,481,10293,20,9139,90,79,481,220,17,92,284,1124,37018,19999,16,19,488,220,20,15170,79,481,220,17,92,284,1124,37018,19999,24,15170,79,481,220,17,532,59,2533,5847,11,582,990,279,1459,1331,35327,1352,315,279,1555,23606,17767,88,481,379,62,16,284,296,2075,481,856,62,16,10699,8,448,279,1459,1124,1188,17,11,481,20,10699,982,59,9640,88,488,220,20,284,1124,37018,19999,24,15170,79,481,220,17,25547,87,481,220,17,340,59,921,50,6383,7766,11,582,633,510,59,9640,88,284,1124,37018,19999,24,15170,79,481,220,17,25547,87,481,220,17,8,481,220,20,198,59,2533,1654,646,1083,990,279,3501,1124,1188,79,11,481,16,19,10699,8,323,1124,1188,79,10,17,11,481,16,22,10699,8,3